{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3870","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3870","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3870\",\"parent_revision\":\"9ad4137bffc7688913fc07c7d7b13cfd35f7dd139fba0bc4c6ea5e6cdf44ceaa\",\"root_revision\":\"9ad4137bffc7688913fc07c7d7b13cfd35f7dd139fba0bc4c6ea5e6cdf44ceaa\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-09-24\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n## Desired outcome\\n\\nOne provider-neutral composition boundary must own the configured primary backend and a reserved local overlay. A reference matching `brief~<mandatory-2-3-word-slug>-<4-lowercase-hex>` must route to the existing project-local SQLite adapter and database; every other reference must use project configuration. The slug must contain two or three meaningful lowercase ASCII words, be truncated only at word boundaries, have no fallback value, and remain immutable with the full reference. The reserved route must never fall back to a remote provider or create a second local store. Callers must not choose providers.\\n\\nThe route must cover work items, content and artifacts, Plans and Tasks, concerns, gates, and completion. Plan creation must atomically bind `plan_id` to backend and Work Brief reference so later plan-addressed operations fail closed through the same route. Mixed listings must retain routing provenance. Collisions are reported through the provider creation contract.\\n\\n## Observed gap and evidence\\n\\nCurrent composition resolves one configured provider. The preflight found no reserved local overlay, cross-state route binding, or mixed-list provenance. #912 owns backend-native Plan storage but not reference-selected overlay routing.\\n\\n## Impact\\n\\nA host-local Work Brief cannot use the normal downstream lifecycle without either switching the project's configured backend or leaking state to the remote provider. Plan-only operations can lose the originating route.\\n\\n## Scope boundaries\\n\\nThis Work Brief owns central composite routing and route provenance. It does not replace #912's TaskBackend storage work, change non-`brief~` identifier selection, switch the global backend, create caller-local prefix branches, add remote fallback, or own creation semantics.\\n\\n## Readiness and acceptance conditions\\n\\nAll approved state families for a valid `brief~` Work Brief resolve to the existing local SQLite store; no remote operation occurs. Invalid or unavailable slugs do not receive a fallback identity. Non-`brief~` references still resolve through configuration. Plan-addressed operations use the atomically stored route, mixed listings identify each record's route, and missing or inconsistent route data fails closed.\\n\\n## Impact\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nA host-local Work Brief cannot use the normal downstream lifecycle without either switching the project's configured backend or leaking state to the remote provider. Plan-only operations can lose the originating route.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: User-confirmed Work Brief grilling session; 2026-09-24 routing preflight\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-09-24\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Desired Outcome\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nOne provider-neutral composition boundary must own the configured primary backend and a reserved local overlay. A reference matching `brief~<mandatory-2-3-word-slug>-<4-lowercase-hex>` must route to the existing project-local SQLite adapter and database; every other reference must use project configuration. The slug must contain two or three meaningful lowercase ASCII words, be truncated only at word boundaries, have no fallback value, and remain immutable with the full reference. The reserved route must never fall back to a remote provider or create a second local store. Callers must not choose providers.\\n\\nThe route must cover work items, content and artifacts, Plans and Tasks, concerns, gates, and completion. Plan creation must atomically bind `plan_id` to backend and Work Brief reference so later plan-addressed operations fail closed through the same route. Mixed listings must retain routing provenance. Collisions are reported through the provider creation contract.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Readiness And Acceptance Conditions\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAll approved state families for a valid `brief~` Work Brief resolve to the existing local SQLite store; no remote operation occurs. Invalid or unavailable slugs do not receive a fallback identity. Non-`brief~` references still resolve through configuration. Plan-addressed operations use the atomically stored route, mixed listings identify each record's route, and missing or inconsistent route data fails closed.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Scope Boundaries\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nThis Work Brief owns central composite routing and route provenance. It does not replace #912's TaskBackend storage work, change non-`brief~` identifier selection, switch the global backend, create caller-local prefix branches, add remote fallback, or own creation semantics.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Observed Gap And Evidence\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nCurrent composition resolves one configured provider. The preflight found no reserved local overlay, cross-state route binding, or mixed-list provenance. #912 owns backend-native Plan storage but not reference-selected overlay routing.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"0b2ac3675f9cb4cdfe73fd1cbb64cdd2d37da71b23b3e6c6c1e27a4c2bde1d4a\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABWnrs0g\"}"}